WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.435
The four cardinal directions are north, east, south and west; a quarter-turn moves to

00:00:05.435 --> 00:00:06.557
the next direction.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:13.214
Face east. Turn a quarter-turn left. Which way now? The answer is north. Use the

00:00:13.214 --> 00:00:15.943
compass order N–E–S–W; after turning, face north.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:22.081
A learner faces east at a market stall and turns one quarter-turn to the right. Which

00:00:22.081 --> 00:00:25.061
direction is faced next? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:31.690
A learner faces east at a market stall and turns one quarter-turn to the right. Which

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:36.785
direction is faced next? The answer is south. Use the compass order N–E–S–W; after

00:00:36.785 --> 00:00:37.877
turning, face south.
